          "cookies": [],
          "content": {
            "size": 43549,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "[{\"categoryIdentifier\":1,\"categoryNameText\":\"Amendment\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"ABST\",\"codeDescription\":\"Abstract\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A portion of the application, as submitted by the applicant, that gives a brief overview of the disclosed invention.\"},{\"codeName\":\"REM\",\"codeDescription\":\"Applicant Arguments/Remarks Made in an Amendment\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A reply by the applicant to an office action must request reconsideration for further examination, must distinctly and specifically point out the supposed errors in the examiner's action and must reply to every ground of objection and rejection in the prior Office action. The reply must present arguments or remarks pointing out the specific distinctions believed to render the claims, including any newly presented claims, patentable over any applied references. In the amendment in reply to a rejection of claims, applicant's arguments or remarks must clearly point out the patentable novelty which he or she thinks the claims present in view of the references cited or the objections made.\"},{\"codeName\":\"CLM\",\"codeDescription\":\"Claims\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The claim is that part of a patent application particularly pointing out and distinctly claiming the subject matter which the applicant regards as the invention or discovery.\"},{\"codeName\":\"DRW\",\"codeDescription\":\"Drawings-only black and white line drawings\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"One or more drawings where necessary for the understanding of the subject matter sought to be patented.\"},{\"codeName\":\"DRW.NONBW\",\"codeDescription\":\"Drawings-other than black and white line drawings\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"One or more drawings where necessary for the understanding of the subject matter sought to be patented.\"},{\"codeName\":\"A.PE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Preliminary Amendment\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Amendment filed by the applicant prior to the Examiner issuing an office action that is based on the merits of the application.\"},{\"codeName\":\"SPEC\",\"codeDescription\":\"Specification\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The written portion of the application is submitted by the applicant describing the invention.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":2,\"categoryNameText\":\"Application Part\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"APP.TXT.PDB\",\"codeDescription\":\"3D Protein Crystals (Text File)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicants may file supplemental protein structure content in PDB-compatible text format (i.e., .txt file) to facilitate prosecution of application.\"},{\"codeName\":\"ABST\",\"codeDescription\":\"Abstract\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A portion of the application, as submitted by the applicant, that gives a brief overview of the disclosed invention.\"},{\"codeName\":\"AF/D.130A\",\"codeDescription\":\"Affidavit-Rule 130(a)-America Invents Act (First Inventor to File) ONLY\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"When any claim of an application or a patent under reexamination is rejected, the applicant or patent owner may submit an appropriate affidavit or declaration to disqualify a disclosure as prior art under Rule 130(a) by establishing that the disclosure was made by the inventor or a joint inventor, or the subject matter disclosed was obtained directly or indirectly from the inventor or a joint inventor.\"},{\"codeName\":\"AF/D.130B\",\"codeDescription\":\"Affidavit-Rule 130(b)-America Invents Act (First Inventor to File) ONLY\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"When any claim of an application or a patent under reexamination is rejected, the applicant or patent owner may submit an appropriate affidavit or declaration to disqualify a disclosure as prior art under Rule 130(b) by establishing that the subject matter disclosed had, before such disclosure was made or before such subject matter was effectively filed, been publicly disclosed by the inventor or a joint inventor or another who obtained the subject matter disclosed directly or indirectly from the inventor or a joint inventor.\"},{\"codeName\":\"AF/D.131\",\"codeDescription\":\"Affidavit-Rule 131-pre-America Invents Act (First to Invent) ONLY\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"When a reference applied by the Examiner has a patent or publication date less than 1 year before the U.S. filing date of the application being examined, applicant may file an affidavit or declaration under Rule 131(a) (Pre-AIA (FTI) Rule 131) to show prior inventorship to overcome the rejection.  When any claim of an application or a patent under reexamination is rejected under 35 U.S.C. 103 on a U.S. patent or U.S. patent application publication which is not prior art under 35 U.S.C. 102(b), and the inventions defined by the claims in the application or patent under reexamination and by the claims in the patent or published application are not identical but are not patentably distinct, and the inventions are owned by the same party, the applicant or owner of the patent under reexamination may disqualify the patent or patent application publication as prior art by submission of an affidavit or declaration under Rule 131(c) (pre-AIA(FTI) Rule 130) stating common ownership and stating that the inventor named is the prior inventor.\"},{\"codeName\":\"AF/D.OTHER\",\"codeDescription\":\"Affidavit-not covered under specific rule\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Evidence submitted by applicant not provided for in the rules.\"},{\"codeName\":\"AF/D.132\",\"codeDescription\":\"Affidavit-traversing rejections or objections rule 132\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Evidence submitted by applicant to overcome a rejection or objection on a basis not otherwise provided for in the rules is submitted as an affidavit under Rule 132.\"},{\"codeName\":\"APPENDIX\",\"codeDescription\":\"Appendix to the specification\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A sequence listing table or a computer program of greater than a specified size must be submitted as an appendix to the specification and be provided on a compact disc.\"},{\"codeName\":\"REM\",\"codeDescription\":\"Applicant Arguments/Remarks Made in an Amendment\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A reply by the applicant to an office action must request reconsideration for further examination, must distinctly and specifically point out the supposed errors in the examiner's action and must reply to every ground of objection and rejection in the prior Office action. The reply must present arguments or remarks pointing out the specific distinctions believed to render the claims, including any newly presented claims, patentable over any applied references. In the amendment in reply to a rejection of claims, applicant's arguments or remarks must clearly point out the patentable novelty which he or she thinks the claims present in view of the references cited or the objections made.\"},{\"codeName\":\"ADS\",\"codeDescription\":\"Application Data Sheet\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The application data sheet is a sheet voluntarily submitted in either provisional or nonprovisional applications and contains bibliographic data, arranged in a format specified by the USPTO in 37 CFR § 1.76. Supplemental application data sheets may be submitted prior to payment of the issue fee either to correct or update information in a previously submitted application data sheet.\"},{\"codeName\":\"CRFS\",\"codeDescription\":\"CRF Statement that Sequence Listing text file (CRF) and paper/pdf Sequence Listing are the same\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"In an application with a “Sequence Listing” submitted on paper or as a pdf file, applicant must submit a copy of the \\\"Sequence Listing\\\" in computer readable form (CRF; i.e. text file). A statement that the content of the paper/pdf copy and the computer readable copy of the \\\"Sequence Listing\\\" are the same is required\"},{\"codeName\":\"APP.TXT.CHEM\",\"codeDescription\":\"Chemical Formulae (Text File)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicants may file supplemental chemical content in InChI text format (i.e., .txt file) to facilitate prosecution of application.\"},{\"codeName\":\"CLM\",\"codeDescription\":\"Claims\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The claim is that part of a patent application particularly pointing out and distinctly claiming the subject matter which the applicant regards as the invention or discovery.\"},{\"codeName\":\"COMPUTER\",\"codeDescription\":\"Computer Listing (Text file)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Computer program listings may be submitted in patent applications when necessary for the purpose of providing the appropriate sequence of instructions, routines, and other contents of a program for a computer. If the computer program listing is sufficiently short, it may be submitted either as drawings or as part of the specification. Longer computer program listings must be submitted on a compact disc. A compact disc containing such a computer program listing is referred to as a \\\".\\\" The not be part of the printed patent.\"},{\"codeName\":\"DRW\",\"codeDescription\":\"Drawings-only black and white line drawings\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"One or more drawings where necessary for the understanding of the subject matter sought to be patented.\"},{\"codeName\":\"DRW.NONBW\",\"codeDescription\":\"Drawings-other than black and white line drawings\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"One or more drawings where necessary for the understanding of the subject matter sought to be patented.\"},{\"codeName\":\"FOR\",\"codeDescription\":\"Foreign Reference\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Foreign references submitted by the applicant for consideration by the examiner.\"},{\"codeName\":\"ECOMM.AUTH\",\"codeDescription\":\"Internet Communications Authorization\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"To communicate with the examiner via internet communications such as email, written authorization is required.  An authorization by the applicant, which authorizes internet communications that has been approved should be coded as ECOMM.AUTH.\"},{\"codeName\":\"R.55.78.STMT\",\"codeDescription\":\"Make/Rescind America Invents Act(AIA) (First Inventor to File) 1.55/1.78 Statement\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"For a nonprovisional application filed on or after March 16, 2013, that claims priority to or the benefit of the filing date of an earlier application (i.e., foreign, provisional, or nonprovisional application, or international application designating the United States of America) that was filed prior to March 16, 2013, and contains, or contained at any time, a claim to a claimed invention that has an effective filing date on or after March 16, 2013, the applicant must provide a statement (under Rule 55 or 78) to that effect within the later of four months from the actual filing date of the later-filed application, four months from the date of entry into the national stage in an international application, sixteen months from the filing date of the prior-filed application, or the date that a first claim to a claimed invention that has an effective filing date on or after March 16, 2013, is presented in the application.  If applicant inadvertently filed such a statement under Rule 55 or 78, applicant may rescind that statement.  The filing receipt must reflect the presence or absence of such a statement under Rule 55 or 78.  Furthermore, the status of the PALM AIA (FITF) indicator may need to be updated (this is not always the case because the status of the PALM AIA (FITF) indicator depends on a number of factors) whenever applicant files such a statement under Rule 55 or 78, or rescinds\"},{\"codeName\":\"APP.TXT.MATH\",\"codeDescription\":\"Mathematical Formulae (Text File)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicants may file supplemental mathematical content in MathML text format (i.e., .txt file) to facilitate prosecution of application.\"},{\"codeName\":\"LET.\",\"codeDescription\":\"Miscellaneous Incoming Letter\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A miscellaneous incoming letter from applicant shall be submitted any time during prosecution that is not directed to a requirement, notice or Office action sent by the USPTO.\"},{\"codeName\":\"NPL\",\"codeDescription\":\"Non Patent Literature\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Non-patent U.S. references submitted by the applicant for consideration by the examiner.\"},{\"codeName\":\"OATH\",\"codeDescription\":\"Oath or Declaration filed\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Each inventor must make an oath or declaration that he/she believes himself/herself to be the original and first inventor of the subject matter of the application, and he/she must make various other statements under 37 CFR § 1.63, As set forth in 37 CFR § 1.64, the oath or declaration must be signed by all of the actual inventors except as provided for in 37 CFR §§ 1.42, 1.43, 1.47, or 1.67.\"},{\"codeName\":\"SPEC\",\"codeDescription\":\"Specification\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The written portion of the application is submitted by the applicant describing the invention.\"},{\"codeName\":\"SPECNO\",\"codeDescription\":\"Specification - Not in English\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The written portion of the application is submitted by the applicant describing the invention that is not submitted in English. Note translation requirements under 37 CFR § 1.52(d).\"},{\"codeName\":\"STAT.DISCLMR\",\"codeDescription\":\"Statutory disclaimers per Manual of Patent Examining Procedure(MPEP) 1490.\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A statement in which a patent owner relinquishes legal rights to one or more claims of a patent. Claims of a patent cannot be disclaimed in favor of new claims to be added to the patent or an amendment to existing claims. (For Example:  PTO/SB/43)\"},{\"codeName\":\"TABLE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Table not included in Specification (Text File)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"In a PCT application, the only tables that may be filed in .txt format are \\\"Tables relating to sequence listing\\\" in accordance with PCT Administrative Instruction Annex C-bis. Document may be included in AS FILED.\"},{\"codeName\":\"DIST\",\"codeDescription\":\"Terminal Disclaimer Filed\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A terminal disclaimer may be filed to overcome non statutory double patenting.\"},{\"codeName\":\"FR TRANS\",\"codeDescription\":\"Translation of Foreign Priority Documents\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"An application may be entitled to the benefit of the filing date of a prior application filed in a foreign country, to overcome an intervening reference or for similar purposes. As part of claiming the benefit of foreign priority, applicant is required to file a certified copy of the original foreign application, specification, and drawings upon which it is based. If the priority papers are not in the English language, a translation is required that may be filed with the priority papers or at a later time.\"},{\"codeName\":\"TRAN.LET\",\"codeDescription\":\"Transmittal Letter\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant provides a transmittal letter such as an Information Disclosure Statement (IDS) letter along with an IDS form (PTO/SB/08) at the earliest possible stage of prosecution detailing the most pertinent references known to applicant.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":4,\"categoryNameText\":\"Change Requests\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"C.AD\",\"codeDescription\":\"Change of Address\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Where an attorney or agent of record (or applicant, if he or she is prosecuting the application pro se) changes his or her correspondence address, he or she is responsible for promptly notifying the USPTO of the new correspondence address (including ZIP Code). The notification should also include his or her telephone number. A change of correspondence address must be signed by an attorney or agent of record.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PA.LIST\",\"codeDescription\":\"List-up to 10 attys appointed in a POA\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Listing of attorney appointed in a POA. List must accompany the PA.. If the power of attorney was already filed (e.g., as part of an oath or declaration), the rule requires that a new copy of the signed document must be filed with separate paper listing the patent practitioners to be entered. If the power of attorney giving power of attorney to more than ten patent practitioners was inadvertently filed without a separate paper listing the patent practitioners to be made of record, the separate listing may be filed subsequently with a cover letter that identifies the power of attorney that has been previously filed and states that all the names on the separate listing appear in the power of attorney, the Office will enter the separate paper listing rather than requiring applicant to resubmit the documents as required in the rule.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PA..\",\"codeDescription\":\"Power of Attorney\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicant may file a change in Power of Attorney at any time during prosecution of an application. The POA indicates representatives given permission to act on behalf of the inventor or assignee to prosecute an application.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PC/I\",\"codeDescription\":\"Power to Make Copies and/or Inspect\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Written authority signed by an applicant, an attorney or agent of record, an authorized official of an assignee or a registered attorney or agent named in the papers accompanying the application papers can be submitted to give access to an application to any person. This written authority gives the named person or persons a power to inspect and make copies of the application. An unrestricted power to inspect given by an applicant is recognized as in effect until rescinded.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":18,\"categoryNameText\":\"Entity Status Correspondence\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"SES.REQ\",\"codeDescription\":\"Assertion of entitlement to small entity status\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"An assertion under 37 CFR 1.27(c) the applicant makes to establish entitlement to a 50% discount of certain fees for filing, searching, examining, issuing, appealing, and maintaining patent applications and patents.  Applicants make small entity status assertions in writing as provided in § 1.27(c)(1), or by payment in the exact amount of one of the small entity basic filing fees represented by fee codes 2011, 4011, 2012, 2017, 2013, 2005, 2014, 2019, and 2631.  To qualify as a small entity, each applicant must be a person, small business concern meeting Small Business Administration standards, or a nonprofit organization as defined in § 1.27(a)(3).  In addition, any party (e.g., applicant, licensee or assignee) holding rights in the application must also qualify as a small entity.\"},{\"codeName\":\"MES.IHEB\",\"codeDescription\":\"Certification of Micro Entity (Education Basis)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A certification under 37 CFR 1.29(d) the applicant files to establish entitlement to a 75% discount of certain fees for filing, searching, examining, issuing, appealing, and maintaining patent applications and patents.  In order to qualify on the institution of higher education basis for the micro entity discount, the applicant must certify that the applicant qualifies as a small entity as defined in 37 CFR 1.27, and that in addition, the applicant meets one of 2 requirements generally referred to as (1) “Employment by an Institution of Higher Education” (from which the applicant obtains the majority of the applicant’s income); or (2) “Assignment or Obligation to Assign to an Institution of Higher Education.”\"},{\"codeName\":\"MES.GIB\",\"codeDescription\":\"Certification of Micro Entity (Gross Income Basis)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A certification under 37 CFR 1.29(a) the applicant files to establish entitlement to a 75% discount of certain fees for filing, searching, examining, issuing, appealing, and maintaining patent applications and patents.  In order to qualify on the gross income basis for the micro entity discount, each inventor and each non-inventor applicant (if any) must meet requirements generally referred to as the Application Filing Limit and the Gross Income Limit.  The same Gross Income Limit applies to any party with an “ownership interest” from any applicant or inventor. In addition, any party (e.g., applicant, licensee or assignee) holding rights in the application must meet the Small Entity Requirement.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":15,\"categoryNameText\":\"First Action Interview Pilot\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"FAI.REQ.INTV\",\"codeDescription\":\"First Action Interview - Schedule Interview request\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant files the request for to schedule the interview under first action interview pilot.\"},{\"codeName\":\"FAI.A..\",\"codeDescription\":\"Reply under 37 CFR 1.111 to Pre-Interview Communication\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicant files a reply in compliance with 37 CFR 1.111 to a Pre-interview Communication. Applicant waives First Action Interview, waives receipt of the First Action Interview Office Action and files a formal amendment.\"},{\"codeName\":\"FAI.REQ.WD\",\"codeDescription\":\"Withdraw Request for First Action Interview\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicants file a communication in response to a Pre-inteview Communication in which applicant requests to not have a first action interview and proceed directly to First Action Interview Office action with no intervening amendment.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":6,\"categoryNameText\":\"General Transmittal\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"L_R IN\",\"codeDescription\":\"Any request going to Licensing and Review\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Requests coming into Licensing and Review include expedited licensing requests for foreign filing, retroactive licensing requests and responses to property rights potential claims from NASA or the Department of Energy.\"},{\"codeName\":\"R3.73\",\"codeDescription\":\"Assignee showing of ownership per 37 CFR 3.73\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"When an assignee to the entire title first seeks to take an action in a patent application, patent or reexamination proceeding, the assignee must file documentary evidence of title as well as a document stating that the evidence has been reviewed and certifying that, to the best of assignee's knowledge and belief, title is in the assignee seeking to take action.\"},{\"codeName\":\"136A\",\"codeDescription\":\"Authorization for Extension of Time all replies\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"37 CFR 1.136 is the patent rule governing extensions of time. A constructive petition for an extension of time should be document indexed as 136A, and is treated as requesting an extension of time for any paper needing an extension of time to be treated as timely filed. In accordance with 37 CFR 1.136(a)(3), there are two types of deposit account authorizations that may be treated as a constructive petition for time for any concurrent or future reply.\"},{\"codeName\":\"SREXR141\",\"codeDescription\":\"Authorization or Rescission of Authorization to Access Search Results\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"For applications subsequently filed in the EPO, the EPO’s Rule 141 EPC (European Patent Convention) requires the applicants to submit a copy of the search results from the U.S. priority application to the EPO if the EPO application is filed on or after January 1, 2011.  This written authorization (Form PTO/SB/69) must be submitted prior to the filing of a subsequent EPO application, in which priority is claimed to a U.S. patent application. No fee will be charged for applicant’s authorization to provide the EPO access to the search results for the application.\"},{\"codeName\":\"CRFS\",\"codeDescription\":\"CRF Statement that Sequence Listing text file (CRF) and paper/pdf Sequence Listing are the same\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"In an application with a “Sequence Listing” submitted on paper or as a pdf file, applicant must submit a copy of the \\\"Sequence Listing\\\" in computer readable form (CRF; i.e. text file). A statement that the content of the paper/pdf copy and the computer readable copy of the \\\"Sequence Listing\\\" are the same is required\"},{\"codeName\":\"XT/\",\"codeDescription\":\"Extension of Time\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"If applicant is required to respond within a shortened statutory time, the applicant may extend that period up to the maximum 6 month period set by statute by filing a written request and the appropriate fee.\"},{\"codeName\":\"WFEE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Fee Worksheet (SB06)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Patent Application Fee Determination Record (Substitute for Form PTO-875)\"},{\"codeName\":\"ECOMM.AUTH\",\"codeDescription\":\"Internet Communications Authorization\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"To communicate with the examiner via internet communications such as email, written authorization is required.  An authorization by the applicant, which authorizes internet communications that has been approved should be coded as ECOMM.AUTH.\"},{\"codeName\":\"ECOMM.WTDW\",\"codeDescription\":\"Internet Communications Authorization Withdrawal\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"To communicate with the examiner via internet communications such as email, written authorization is required.  To withdraw authorization, written authorization is also required.  A withdrawal of authorization by the applicant, which withdraws authorization for internet communications that is approved should be coded as ECOMM.AUTH.WTDW\"},{\"codeName\":\"M865\",\"codeDescription\":\"Letter Requesting Interview with Examiner\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Interviews with examiners concerning applications and other matters pending before the Office must be conducted on Office premises and within Office hours. An interview should normally be arranged for in advance, as by letter or telephone call, in order to insure that the primary examiner and/or the examiner in charge of the application will be present and available in the Office.\"},{\"codeName\":\"M856\",\"codeDescription\":\"Letter Requesting Suspension of Action\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"An applicant may file a petition to suspend action in an application for a specific period of time for good and sufficient reasons. An example would be where a request for continued examination is made before a preliminary amendment is filed. The suspension would be requested to prevent having the case examined before the preliminary amendment is entered.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PA.LIST\",\"codeDescription\":\"List-up to 10 attys appointed in a POA\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Listing of attorney appointed in a POA. List must accompany the PA.. If the power of attorney was already filed (e.g., as part of an oath or declaration), the rule requires that a new copy of the signed document must be filed with separate paper listing the patent practitioners to be entered. If the power of attorney giving power of attorney to more than ten patent practitioners was inadvertently filed without a separate paper listing the patent practitioners to be made of record, the separate listing may be filed subsequently with a cover letter that identifies the power of attorney that has been previously filed and states that all the names on the separate listing appear in the power of attorney, the Office will enter the separate paper listing rather than requiring applicant to resubmit the documents as required in the rule.\"},{\"codeName\":\"LET.\",\"codeDescription\":\"Miscellaneous Incoming Letter\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A miscellaneous incoming letter from applicant shall be submitted any time during prosecution that is not directed to a requirement, notice or Office action sent by the USPTO.\"},{\"codeName\":\"EXPD.LICENSE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition for Expedited Foreign Filing Licenses\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The Office of License and Review (L&R) offers a service to Petition for Expedited Foreign Filing License. The Office will render a decision on the petition within 3 business days.  The Petitions are received by hand carry, facsimile directly in L&R, or via EFS-Web.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PA..\",\"codeDescription\":\"Power of Attorney\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicant may file a change in Power of Attorney at any time during prosecution of an application. The POA indicates representatives given permission to act on behalf of the inventor or assignee to prosecute an application.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PRO.BON.CERT\",\"codeDescription\":\"Pro Bono Representation Certification\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A certification to be filed by an attorney in a new or pending application certifying that the application is being prosecuted pro bono\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.RELIEF\",\"codeDescription\":\"Relief in Emergency Situations Determined by Director\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"​A petition filed during a natural disaster (e.g. Katrina, Japan Tsunami, Covid). SB/425, 453\"},{\"codeName\":\"TRAN.LET\",\"codeDescription\":\"Transmittal Letter\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant provides a transmittal letter such as an Information Disclosure Statement (IDS) letter along with an IDS form (PTO/SB/08) at the earliest possible stage of prosecution detailing the most pertinent references known to applicant.\"},{\"codeName\":\"TRNA\",\"codeDescription\":\"Transmittal of New Application\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A transmittal letter for a new application indicating the contents of the submission, including any accompanying fees.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":7,\"categoryNameText\":\"IDS/References\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"IDS.SIZEFEE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Assertion regarding Information Disclosure Statement (IDS) Size Fee (SB/08C)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant provides an Information Disclosure Statement (IDS) at the earliest possible stage of prosecution detailing the most pertinent references known to applicant. The Examiner is to consider each reference cited in the IDS prior to the next Office action on the merits. Each IDS must be accompanied by a written assertion under 37 CFR 1.98 and the appropriate size fee under 37 CFR 1.17(v).\"},{\"codeName\":\"FOR\",\"codeDescription\":\"Foreign Reference\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Foreign references submitted by the applicant for consideration by the examiner.\"},{\"codeName\":\"IDS\",\"codeDescription\":\"Information Disclosure Statement (IDS) Form (SB08)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant provides an Information Disclosure Statement (IDS) at the earliest possible stage of prosecution detailing the most pertinent references known to applicant. The Examiner is to considered each reference cited in the IDS prior to the next Office action on the merits.\"},{\"codeName\":\"NPL\",\"codeDescription\":\"Non Patent Literature\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Non-patent U.S. references submitted by the applicant for consideration by the examiner.\"},{\"codeName\":\"REF.OTHER\",\"codeDescription\":\"Other reference-Patent/Application/Search Documents\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Submission of US Patent, US Application documentation or International or Foreign Search Reports\"},{\"codeName\":\"PTA.IDS\",\"codeDescription\":\"Patent Term Adjustment Statement under 37 CFR 1.704(d) filed with an IDS\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Statement filed with an IDS when the references were first cited in any communication from a patent office in a counterpart foreign or international application or from the Office, and this communication was not received by any individual designated in § 1.56(c) more than thirty days prior to the filing of the information disclosure statement; or the references are communications that were issued by a patent office in a counterpart foreign or international application or by the Office, and this communication was not received by any individual designated in § 1.56(c) more than thirty days prior to the filing of the information disclosure statement\"},{\"codeName\":\"TRAN.LET\",\"codeDescription\":\"Transmittal Letter\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant provides a transmittal letter such as an Information Disclosure Statement (IDS) letter along with an IDS form (PTO/SB/08) at the earliest possible stage of prosecution detailing the most pertinent references known to applicant.\"},{\"codeName\":\"IDS.R197.REL\",\"codeDescription\":\"​Letter specifying the conditions for filing under 37 CFR 1.97​\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant provides an Information Disclosure Statement (IDS) letter along with an IDS form (PTO/SB/08) specifying the conditions for filing the IDS under 37CFR1.97 and explaining the relevance of the references citied under 37CFR1.98(a)(3)(i)​\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":9,\"categoryNameText\":\"Office of Patent Pub\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"PG.NONPUB.RQ\",\"codeDescription\":\"Nonpublication request from applicant\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A nonpublication request must be submitted with the application upon filing, certifying that the invention disclosed in the application has not been and will not be the subject of an application filed in another country, or under a multilateral international agreement, that requires publication at eighteen months after filing. Form PTO/SB/35 may be used by applicant for filing this request.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":10,\"categoryNameText\":\"Petition\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"PET.COLOR\",\"codeDescription\":\"A petition from Applicant to accept Color Drawings or Color Photographs\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Petition from Applicant to accept color drawings or color photographs\"},{\"codeName\":\"SC.RH.PET\",\"codeDescription\":\"Incoming - Petition for Rehearing - Supreme Court\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Petitioner files a Petition for Rehearing where Petition for Writ of Certiorari was denied in the Supreme Court\"},{\"codeName\":\"SC.RH.PETD\",\"codeDescription\":\"Incoming - Petition for Rehearing Denied - Supreme Court\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Supreme Court issues a decision/order denying the Petition for Rehearing filed by Petitioner.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.PTA\",\"codeDescription\":\"Patent Term Adjustment Petition\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"An incoming petition from applicant is sent to the official who has been delegated with the authority to decide the petition. Some petitions are delegated to the Office of Petitions to act on the decision or continue prosecution.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.OPLA\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition decided by Patent Legal Administration\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.ASPILOT\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition for Automated Search Pilot\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The request is submitted by applicant to participate in the Automated Search Pilot Program.  The request must be submitted with or after the electronic filing of an original utility nonprovisional application no later than September 30, 2025, wherein the specification, claim(s), and abstract of the application are in DOCX format on filing.  The request is decided by OITP before an application is examined\"},{\"codeName\":\"EXPD.LICENSE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition for Expedited Foreign Filing Licenses\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The Office of License and Review (L&R) offers a service to Petition for Expedited Foreign Filing License. The Office will render a decision on the petition within 3 business days.  The Petitions are received by hand carry, facsimile directly in L&R, or via EFS-Web.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.OP\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition for review by the Office of Petitions\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"An incoming petition from applicant is sent to the official who has been delegated with the authority to decide the petition. Some petitions are delegated to the Office of Petitions to act on the decision or continue prosecution.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.PCT\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition for review by the PCT legal office\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"An incoming petition from applicant is sent to the official who has been delegated with the authority to decide the petition. Some petitions are delegated to the Patent Cooperation Treaty Legal Administrator to act on the decision or continue prosecution.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.SPRE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition for review by the Technology Center Special Program Examiner(SPRE)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"An incoming petition from applicant is sent to the official who has been delegated with the authority to decide the petition. Some petitions are delegated to the Technology Center Special Program Examiner to act on the decision or continue prosecution.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.CSP\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition to Make Special for Collaborative Search\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Petition to make special based on the collaborative search program\"},{\"codeName\":\"PPH.PET.652\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition to make Special under Patent Prosecution Highway\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicant uses the request/petition form to request participation in the Patent Prosecution Highway (PPH) pilot program. The request form has a check list of all the requirements and the use of the form will ensure that all requirements are met.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.SPARKAPP\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition to make application special under the SPARK pilot\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant files a petition requesting that examination of an application be expedited. The petition is decided in accordance with the requirements of the SPARK pilot program.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.OP.AGE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition to make special based on Age\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"An incoming petition from applicant delegated to the Office of Petitions to act on the decision or continue prosecution. This petition is requesting to be made special because of advanced age (over 65 years of age) or poor health.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.RELIEF\",\"codeDescription\":\"Relief in Emergency Situations Determined by Director\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"​A petition filed during a natural disaster (e.g. Katrina, Japan Tsunami, Covid). SB/425, 453\"},{\"codeName\":\"CERT.AC.HM.R\",\"codeDescription\":\"Request Acceleration Certificate Humanitarian Program\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"When an owner of an Acceleration Certificate under the Humanitarian Awards Pilot Program desires to redeem the Acceleration Certificate and accelerate Office processing for a pending application or reexamination proceeding, the owner completes and files the CERT.AC.HM.R form.  The Office form is recommended, but the owner’s own form may be used at Owner’s risk.  The form must identify the unique Certificate Number being redeemed and the application or reexamination proceeding number for which acceleration is being sought.  Upon receipt and review of the Redemption Request the Office will determine whether to grant or dismiss acceleration.  If previous Redemption Request has been dismissed, then a new Redemption Request may be filed.\"},{\"codeName\":\"RETR.LICENSE\",\"codeDescription\":\"Request for Retroactive Foreign Filing License\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.POA.WDRW\",\"codeDescription\":\"Request for withdrawal as attorney or agent\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Incoming petition to withdraw the attorney or agent and change the address. PTO form AIA/83 is used for withdrawing.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":16,\"categoryNameText\":\"Pilot Programs\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"REQ.MIS.PART\",\"codeDescription\":\"Certification and Request for Missing Parts\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.ASPILOT\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition for Automated Search Pilot\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The request is submitted by applicant to participate in the Automated Search Pilot Program.  The request must be submitted with or after the electronic filing of an original utility nonprovisional application no later than September 30, 2025, wherein the specification, claim(s), and abstract of the application are in DOCX format on filing.  The request is decided by OITP before an application is examined\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.CSP\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition to Make Special for Collaborative Search\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Petition to make special based on the collaborative search program\"},{\"codeName\":\"PPH.PET.652\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition to make Special under Patent Prosecution Highway\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicant uses the request/petition form to request participation in the Patent Prosecution Highway (PPH) pilot program. The request form has a check list of all the requirements and the use of the form will ensure that all requirements are met.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PET.SPARKAPP\",\"codeDescription\":\"Petition to make application special under the SPARK pilot\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The applicant files a petition requesting that examination of an application be expedited. The petition is decided in accordance with the requirements of the SPARK pilot program.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PEER.CONSENT\",\"codeDescription\":\"Request for Peer Review\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The patent owner/assignee/applicant presents the form according to the provisions of the Peer to patent pilot to allow the application to be apart of the program.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":8,\"categoryNameText\":\"Pre-Exam\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"REQ.MIS.PART\",\"codeDescription\":\"Certification and Request for Missing Parts\"},{\"codeName\":\"PG.NONPUB.RQ\",\"codeDescription\":\"Nonpublication request from applicant\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"A nonpublication request must be submitted with the application upon filing, certifying that the invention disclosed in the application has not been and will not be the subject of an application filed in another country, or under a multilateral international agreement, that requires publication at eighteen months after filing. Form PTO/SB/35 may be used by applicant for filing this request.\"},{\"codeName\":\"PEER.CONSENT\",\"codeDescription\":\"Request for Peer Review\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"The patent owner/assignee/applicant presents the form according to the provisions of the Peer to patent pilot to allow the application to be apart of the program.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":11,\"categoryNameText\":\"Pre-Grant Pub\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"EARLYPUB\",\"codeDescription\":\"Request for Early Publication\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applications are normally published 18 months after they are filed. Applicant may request that his or her application be published earlier than that date.\"}]},{\"categoryIdentifier\":14,\"categoryNameText\":\"Priority Documents\",\"categoryDescriptionText\":null,\"documentCodeBag\":[{\"codeName\":\"PD.TO.AUTH\",\"codeDescription\":\"Authorization or Rescission of Authorization to Access Application by Digital Access Service /Priority Document Exchange Office\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"This document is an authorization from a US applicant permitting access to their electronic US Patent Applications by participating International Offices.\"},{\"codeName\":\"FRPR.IC\",\"codeDescription\":\"Interim Copy of the Foreign Priority Document\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Applicant may file an interim copy of the foreign priority document in order to meet the time period requirement to file a certified copy in Rule 55 for applications filed on or after March 16, 2013.  An interim copy is a true copy from the applicant’s record of the foreign priority application as originally filed with the foreign office and is not a copy of the certified copy.  See Rule 55 for requirements of an interim copy.  A certified copy of the foreign priority document is required before patent grant in order to be entitled to foreign priority.  An interim copy does not satisfy the certified copy requirement.\"},{\"codeName\":\"FRPR.IC.TXT\",\"codeDescription\":\"Interim Copy of the Foreign Priority Document (Text file)\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Interim copy of Foreign Priority Document (text file)\"},{\"codeName\":\"PD.REQ.RETR\",\"codeDescription\":\"Request for USPTO to retrieve priority docs\",\"extendedDescriptionText\":\"Request from the applicant authorizing the USPTO to electronically retrieve Official Priority Documents from participating foreign IP Office and enter them into the file wrapper.\"}]}]"
          },
